<title>USA: Global Industrial to sell units, sees loss.</title>
<headline>Global Industrial to sell units, sees loss.</headline>
<dateline>DALLAS 1997-01-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Global Industrial Technologies Inc said it will divest a number of business units that do not fit its long-term strategic plan, and as a result it will report a first quarter loss ranging from $0.50-0.53 a share.</p>
<p>Global said it will report a loss after it has recognized a pre-tax charge of $20.5 million in the first quarter in connection with the divestitures, which includes a foreign exchange loss on the investments of $7.7 million.</p>
<p>Global said that it estimates a loss for the first quarter of between $11.3-$12 million. Excluding the charge, Global expects to report earnings of $0.15 to $0.18 a share.</p>
</text>
